Use `@testing-library/react-native` for component and hook testing.

Prefer testing behavior over implementation details.

Avoid:

- testing internal state
- testing private methods
- snapshot-heavy testing

Prefer:

- user interactions
- accessible queries
- realistic rendering flows

## Installation

```bash
npm install -D @testing-library/react-native jest jest-expo
```

## Basic Component Test

```tsx
import { render, screen } from "@testing-library/react-native";

import { Button } from "@/components/button";

describe("Button", () => {
  it("renders correctly", () => {
    render(<Button title="Save" />);

    expect(screen.getByText("Save")).toBeTruthy();
  });
});
```

## User Interaction

Prefer `userEvent` over `fireEvent` when possible.

```tsx
import { render, screen, userEvent } from "@testing-library/react-native";

it("submits form", async () => {
  const onSubmit = jest.fn();

  const user = userEvent.setup();

  render(<LoginForm onSubmit={onSubmit} />);

  await user.type(screen.getByLabelText("Email"), "john@mail.com");

  await user.press(
    screen.getByRole("button", {
      name: "Submit",
    }),
  );

  expect(onSubmit).toHaveBeenCalled();
});
```

## Hook Testing

Use `renderHook` for custom hooks.

```tsx
import { act, renderHook } from "@testing-library/react-native";

import { useCounter } from "@/hooks/use-counter";

it("increments counter", () => {
  const { result } = renderHook(() => useCounter());

  act(() => {
    result.current.increment();
  });

  expect(result.current.count).toBe(1);
});
```

## Queries

Prefer accessible queries.

Priority:

1. `getByRole`
2. `getByLabelText`
3. `getByText`
4. `getByPlaceholderText`
5. `getByTestId` as last resort

```tsx
screen.getByRole("button", {
  name: "Continue",
});
```

## Async Testing

Use `findBy*` and `waitFor` for async UI.

```tsx
import { render, screen, waitFor } from "@testing-library/react-native";

it("loads users", async () => {
  render(<UsersScreen />);

  expect(screen.getByText("Loading")).toBeTruthy();

  await waitFor(() => {
    expect(screen.getByText("John")).toBeTruthy();
  });
});
```

## Custom Render

Prefer a shared render helper for providers.

```tsx
import { render } from "@testing-library/react-native";

function Providers({ children }) {
  return children;
}

export function renderWithProviders(component: React.ReactNode) {
  return render(component, {
    wrapper: Providers,
  });
}
```

## Best Practices

- Test behavior instead of implementation
- Prefer screen queries over container access
- Keep tests small and focused
- Avoid excessive mocking
- Avoid snapshot-heavy testing
- Prefer accessibility-first queries
- Use `renderHook` for isolated hook testing
- Use async queries for async UI
- Prefer reusable render helpers
